1
00:00:00,105 --> 00:00:01,252
(Q11（Diagram）) Hello?

2
00:00:01,252 --> 00:00:01,983
Hi.

3
00:00:01,983 --> 00:00:03,683
It's Laura Carlton here.

4
00:00:03,683 --> 00:00:08,755
We've just arrived at the holiday flat, but I can't get the hot water and heating to work.

5
00:00:08,755 --> 00:00:10,295
Oh right!

6
00:00:10,295 --> 00:00:12,616
That's easy. Don't worry.

7
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


8
00:00:12,616 --> 00:00:16,155
In the upstairs cupboard, you'll find the water heater.

9
00:00:16,155 --> 00:00:20,466
You'll see three main controls on the left at the bottom of the heater.

10
00:00:20,466 --> 00:00:27,107
The first one-the round one on the far left-is the most important one for the heating and hot water.

11
00:00:27,107 --> 00:00:29,133
It's the main control switch.

12
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:31,612
Make sure it's in the 'on' position.

13
00:00:31,612 --> 00:00:37,831
The switch itself doesn't light up, but the little square below will be black if the switch is 'off'.

14
00:00:37,831 --> 00:00:42,195
That's probably what's happened-it's got switched off by mistake.

15
00:00:42,195 --> 00:00:49,223
[控制旋钮] The middle one of these three controls-you'll see it's slightly larger than the first one-controls the radiators.

16
00:00:49,223 --> 00:00:55,314
If you feel cold while you're there and need the radiators on, this needs to be turned to maximum.

17
00:00:55,314 --> 00:01:05,178
The last of the three controls-the one on the right-is usually on about a number for setting which for the water in the taps is usually quite hot enough.

18
00:01:05,178 --> 00:01:10,556
Below the heating controls in the middle is a small round plastic button.

19
00:01:10,556 --> 00:01:15,219
If there isn't enough water in the pipes, sometimes the heater goes out.

20
00:01:15,219 --> 00:01:19,287
If this happens you'll need to press this button to reset the heater.

21
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:24,546
Hold it in for about five seconds and the heater should come on again.

22
00:01:24,546 --> 00:01:30,481
Then there's a little square indicator under the third knob that's a kind of alarm light.

23
00:01:30,481 --> 00:01:32,915
It'll flash if you need to reset the heater.

24
00:01:32,915 --> 00:01:35,693
It sounds complicated…

25
00:01:35,693 --> 00:01:38,762
I'm sure you won't have any problems with it.

26
00:01:38,762 --> 00:01:42,677
There should be some more instructions on the side of the heater.

27
00:01:42,677 --> 00:01:44,788
Call me back if you can't make it work.

28
00:01:44,788 --> 00:01:48,013
Okay.

29
00:01:48,013 --> 00:01:56,297
(Q14（配对）) [生活用品] While you're on the phone, we haven't managed to find a few things we need, like extra pillows for the beds and some washing powder.

30
00:01:56,297 --> 00:01:57,920
Is there any here?

31
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:10,438
(Q14) [Q14答案句B： cupboard原词，可能的Q14干扰项 E (shelf), F(top)，但定语都不对] Pillows… yes. If you look in the cupboard, the large white one upstairs-to the left of the bathroom door-there should be four or five on the top shelf.

32
00:02:10,438 --> 00:02:16,201
(Q15) And if you want to do some washing, there's some powder for that…

33
00:02:16,201 --> 00:02:21,944
[Q15答案句E： by the back door原词，shelf原词] probably by the back door. There's a kind of shelf there above the sink.

34
00:02:21,944 --> 00:02:25,455
[Q15干扰项A：提到了 box, 但位置不对，没有on washing machine] In fact, I'm sure there's some there, in a large blue box.

35
00:02:25,455 --> 00:02:29,095
You need about half a cup full for each wash.

36
00:02:29,095 --> 00:02:37,066
(Q16) [Q16答案句D：next to = by, window原词] And that reminds me, the spare key to the back door is hanging on a hook on the wall by the sitting room window.

37
00:02:37,066 --> 00:02:40,028
Please make sure to put it back when you've used it.

38
00:02:40,028 --> 00:02:44,189
The previous guests lost it in the garden and I had to get another one made!

39
00:02:44,189 --> 00:02:55,235
(Q17) [Q17答案句A：box 原词+ on top of washing machine 原词] And if you have any trouble with the lamps,you'll find some spare bulbs in a large cardboard box. It's on top of the washing machine with all kinds of useful things in it.

40
00:02:55,235 --> 00:02:58,706
(Q18) Oh, and another thing I forgot to mention when we last spoke…

41
00:02:58,706 --> 00:02:59,822
Yes?

42
00:02:59,822 --> 00:03:04,068
I've left you a local map, so you'll be able to find your way around easily.

43
00:03:04,068 --> 00:03:06,247
It shows the whole area.

44
00:03:06,247 --> 00:03:10,593
[Q18答案句C： drawer of the chest = in the chest of drawers 语序颠倒一下] I put it in the top drawer of the chest under the TV in your bedroom.

45
00:03:10,593 --> 00:03:13,865
There's a whole file of local information in there too.

46
00:03:13,865 --> 00:03:14,820
(Q19（notes）) Thanks.

47
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:16,995
What about visiting the town?

48
00:03:16,995 --> 00:03:18,559
Can you give us any advice?

49
00:03:18,559 --> 00:03:19,932
Yes.

50
00:03:19,932 --> 00:03:22,152
You'll need to take the car.

51
00:03:22,152 --> 00:03:24,864
It's too far to talk from the flat really.

52
00:03:24,864 --> 00:03:34,793
You have to pay to leave your car in all the car parks now I'm afraid…I like the one that's by the station best and you can walk to the town centre from there in five minutes.

53
00:03:34,793 --> 00:03:37,205
That's where all the best restaurants are.

54
00:03:37,205 --> 00:03:42,397
[外卖选择] But if you want a takeaway, the ltalian one does really good pasta and pizzas.

55
00:03:42,397 --> 00:03:51,754
Call 7-3 double 2,8-1for that one, or 7 double 6, double 1, 9 for the Chinese.

56
00:03:51,754 --> 00:03:55,162
They're both good and they'll both deliver to the flat.

57
00:03:55,162 --> 00:04:01,330
[铁路博物馆] As for places to visit, yes, do go and see the railway museum.

58
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:04,657
The exhibition is small but really good.

59
00:04:04,657 --> 00:04:20,448
It gets very crowded on Sundays, so I suggest you visit it on a quieter day, later in the week, but not on Thursdays which is market day-you won't find anywhere to park and it's also the only day of the week when they're not open!

60
00:04:20,448 --> 00:04:21,825
Anything else?

61
00:04:21,825 --> 00:04:22,822
Not for the moment.

62
00:04:22,822 --> 00:04:25,322
Thanks!

